WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.570
People are getting sick

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.705
we we should not have been, like,

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:06.806
back into town

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.875
until all of this was done.

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:12.212
This morning, people in East

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.880
Palestine, Ohio,

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.348
scared the toxic chemicals

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.316
from a massive train

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:17.350
derailment are putting

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.119
their lives at risk.

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.120
CNN has obtained

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.322
new videos of the train before the crash,

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:23.289
and they're helping us

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.425
pieced together a timeline.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:27.160
So let's check out some of this.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.028
First,
you see videos

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:29.863
from along the train tracks

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:32.098
This is in Alliance, Ohio,

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:33.900
and you see the train passing.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.935
This is on the right side of your screen.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.137
Now, this was about 15.

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:38.705
This was about 57 minutes

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:39.606
before the crash.

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:41.941
And you can see there are no sparks.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.044
The train keeps heading down the tracks.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.546
And by eight, 12 p.m.

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:47.714
it's in Salem.

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:49.983
Now you can see

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:51.918
sparks from an apparent wheel

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:54.621
bearing overheating.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.556
Here's another surveillance camera.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:59.325
Same time, same town.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:02.028
The train keeps going for 20 miles

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:02.996
after that point.

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:06.032
Headed for East Palestine.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.935
And that is where it derails at eight 55.

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.870
A full 43 minutes

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.605
after we saw those sparks.

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:13.807
And Salem.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.009
CNN's Jason Carroll is live

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:17.477
in East Palestine.

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:18.211
And Jason,

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.212
we just want to start with

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:21.147
what the NTSB is saying

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:25.051
about the video and the investigation

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:27.887
Well, this is clearly going to be a key

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.789
part of the investigation

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:32.759
into what exactly went wrong out here.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.527
And according to the NTSB,

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.362
that surveillance video

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.530
that you just referenced there

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.232
and I'm going to quote here, appears

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.266
to show a wheel

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:41.935
bearing in the final stage

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:44.070
of overheat failure.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.673
Moments before the derailment.

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:48.108
Now, of course, that wheel bearing

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:49.642
is a key component.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:52.045
Hopes to connect the wheel to the axle.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:53.379
The parts in question

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.181
have all been collected

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:56.816
They've been examined.

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:57.817
They're going to be taken

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.686
now to Washington, D.C.,

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:00.420
where they will be

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.755
examined by investigators

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:05.391
there at a laboratory with the NTSB.

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:06.259
We should also tell you,

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:07.861
Audie, that the NTSB

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:09.129
has also collected

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:11.431
the locomotive event recorder.

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.433
That is also going to be key

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:14.334
to the investigation

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:15.602
going forward in Turin

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.103
in terms of trying to determine

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.571
exactly what went wrong.

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:21.841
Now, the EPA administrator

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.943
actually was visiting East Palestine

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.745
and you got to speak with him.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:27.380
What did he tell you

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:29.949
Well, it was a short

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:30.917
conversation,

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:33.052
but an important conversation.

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:35.522
The EPA administrator, Michael Regan,

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:36.689
made it very clear

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:37.423
that he knows

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:38.825
that people are scared,

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:39.893
that they are very worried

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:41.261
about their health.

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:42.829
He also said that he knows that

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.430
people do not trust the government

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.131
when they say that

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:47.500
the air and the water is safe.

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:50.270
Here's more of what he had to say.

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:51.304
You've heard

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.539
some of the stories that are coming

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:53.072
in, people

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:53.907
talking about

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:55.308
having rashes, their pets

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:56.876
getting sick, things like that.

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:57.977
What I would say is

00:02:57.977 --> 00:02:59.479
if anyone is experiencing

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:02.148
any kind of adverse symptoms,

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:04.784
have their pets go to the veterinarian?

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.486
They should seek medical attention.

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.521
We need for this information

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:10.423
to get to the state health department

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:12.058
so that we can coordinate

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:13.059
and be sure that people

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.460
are getting the help that they need

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.528
to help us clear up

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.397
what specifically you're testing for.

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:19.632
Is it just for vinyl chloride?

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:21.734
We are testing for the full breadth

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:22.936
of toxic chemicals

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:25.104
that were on that train that was spilled.

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:27.473
We have the capabilities to detect

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.542
every single adverse impact

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:31.211
that would result from that spill.

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:32.045
And that's what we're doing.

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:33.413
We will be here

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:35.315
for as long as it takes

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:36.983
to see this process through.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:38.384
I want to assure the people

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:39.919
I just want to say,

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:41.354
when you say as long as it takes,

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:42.822
I think the question is long

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.490
term, is someone going to be here

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.458
a year from now,

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:47.193
two years from now to come back?

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:49.195
Test the water, test the soil.

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:52.432
I'm very clear when I say as long

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:53.900
as it takes,

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.102
we will go through this process.

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:58.705
With the citizens of East Palestine

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:00.773
for as long as it takes.

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.075
The federal government will be here

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:04.777
for as long as it takes.

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:08.248
So, again, you heard it there, Audie.

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:08.848
The EPA

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:09.949
administrator says

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.451
as long as it takes,

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:13.453
whatever that ends up being.

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:14.354
Also want to tell you

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:15.989
that Ohio's governor

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:18.324
has asked the CDC to get involved.

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:19.959
He wants CDC experts

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:21.027
here on the ground

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:21.661
to examine

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.930
people who say they are having symptoms

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:24.631
Audie.

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:25.632
Jason Carroll,

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:26.833
thank you for your reporting.

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:27.533
Joining us now

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:28.434
is the water quality

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:28.935
and treatment

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:30.270
superintendent of Greater

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:31.771
Cincinnati Waterworks,

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:33.006
Jeff Sweat for her.

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:33.906
Thank you so much.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:34.974
You serve more than a million

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:36.476
people in the Cincinnati area.

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:38.411
You get 88% of the drinking

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:39.712
water from the Ohio River.

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:40.613
So that's obviously

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:42.315
why so many people have questions.

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:44.050
I know you've been doing testing.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.019
What exactly do you test for?

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:47.153
What does that look like?

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:49.989
So we're working with

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:51.190
a lot of partners

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.458
here, with regional partners

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:53.860
from U.S., EPA, Ohio,

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.094
and especially or Sankoh,

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:56.129
the Ohio River Valley Water

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:57.397
Sanitation Commission.

00:04:57.397 --> 00:04:58.264
So we're going.

00:04:58.264 --> 00:04:59.532
We're working with that group,

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:00.300
getting samples

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.235
from all of them down the Ohio River.

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:04.337
We're bringing in here into our lab

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:05.605
and doing these analysis.

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:07.040
Now, fortunately,

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.675
we're not finding the high concentrations

00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:10.576
that they're seeing up in up in the East

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:12.111
Palestine area.

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:14.280
Our concentrations are much less.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.049
And as it's coming down the Ohio River,

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:17.216
what we're seeing is

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:18.951
especially one compound

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:19.886
that what's been detected

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:21.120
is called futile accolade.

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:22.388
that compound

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:23.589
is actually decreasing a bit

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:24.791
as it's coming down the river

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:27.660
between its apologizing being up, but

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:29.095
the concentration

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:29.929
becoming less and less

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:31.364
as it's moving towards us.

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:32.265
So it's becoming less

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:32.665
and less

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:34.400
that you are seeing a difference, though,

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.169
since this train wreck has happened.

00:05:37.704 --> 00:05:38.671
Yeah.
So this is something

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:40.440
that we would not have detected before,

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.442
but we would the test that we do.

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:43.509
We have a suite of tests

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:44.911
that we do all the time

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:45.611
anyway to make sure

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:46.245
that the water's safe.

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.080
So if there's anything in there

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.115
we don't know about or detect it.

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:49.916
This would,

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:50.483
this compound

00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:51.751
would have been detected in that.

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:52.819
And we don't detect it

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:54.187
because we haven't detected before.

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:56.389
But now we're detecting upstream of

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:58.691
of the city, Cincinnati.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:05:59.125
One thing,

00:05:59.125 --> 00:05:59.792
Jeff, that we've heard

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:01.160
from a lot of people is

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.029
they're skeptical of the testing

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.130
I know we hear from you.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.298
We've heard from officials in East

00:06:05.298 --> 00:06:05.898
Palestine

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:07.767
